\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. A way with our fears!
\par The glad morning appears
\par When an heir of salvation was born!
\par From Jehovah I came,
\par For His glory I am,
\par And to Him I with singing return.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. I sing of Thy grace,
\par From my earliest days
\par Ever near to allure and defend;
\par Hitherto Thou hast been
\par My Preserver from sin,
\par And I trust Thou wilt save to the end.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. O the infinite cares,
\par And temptations, and snares
\par Thy hand hath conducted me through!
\par O the blessings bestowed
\par By a bountiful God,
\par And the mercies eternally new!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. What a mercy in this,
\par What a heaven of bliss,
\par How unspeakably happy am I;
\par Gathered into the fold,
\par With Thy people enrolled,
\par With Thy people to live and to die.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

